From 3059a1a53bc8582b1d191c7bd795acae221a80b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 07:33:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate terratern-linktree as a config-driven public page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds public/linktree.html (the public "link in bio" page) and
public/linktree-config.js (all editable content: tagline, stats,
the full link list with icon/title/subtitle/url/badge, and footer)
pulled out of the page into one plain config file, following the
same "edit only this file" convention already used in
terratern-ads-landing-page's config.js.

This is a standalone public page — no shell/sidebar wrap, since it's
a public marketing link people tap from social bios, not an internal
CRM tool. To change what it shows, edit public/linktree-config.js and
push; no build step, database, or live admin UI involved.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LHzxqv9S6k47oG19wZF3Kx
---
 public/linktree-config.js | 105 ++++++++++++
 public/linktree.html      | 351 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 456 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 public/linktree-config.js
 create mode 100644 public/linktree.html

diff --git a/public/linktree-config.js b/public/linktree-config.js
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..00386de
--- /dev/null
+++ b/public/linktree-config.js
@@ -0,0 +1,105 @@
+// ============================================================
+//  TERRATERN LINKTREE — CONFIG FILE
+//  Edit ONLY this file to change the page's stats or links.
+//  Do not touch linktree.html unless you're changing the layout.
+//
+//  Each link:
+//    icon     - emoji shown before the title
+//    title    - bold heading text
+//    subtitle - smaller description line
+//    url      - where the button goes (keep utm params for tracking)
+//    badge    - optional: { text: "Limited Slots", style: "urgent" }
+//               style is "urgent" (red, pulsing) or "normal" (gold).
+//               Omit "badge" entirely for no badge.
+// ============================================================
